\begin{align*}
3 - y - y & = (3 - y - 2) + (y - 2),\\
3 - 2y & = 1 - 2,
\end{align*}
which simplifies to $3 - 2y = -1$. Solving for $y$, we get $2y = 4$, hence $y = 2$. Plugging $y = 2$ into $x = 3 - y$, we find $x = 1$. So, the ordered pair is $\boxed{(1,2)}$. </think> <answer>$\boxed{(1,2)}$</answer>
